      "description": "Embark on a profound journey with \"Quiet Harvest,\" the debut album from The Shady River Bard. This collection of 12 blues-infused country tales weaves a rich tapestry of life lived, wisdom earned, and peace found in the quiet corners of the world.\n\nUpon retiring from corporate life, The Shady River Bard started the Shady River Homestead, LLC., a permaculture farm located on 7 beautiful acres in the Pacific Northwest.  More than a few of his friends asked a simple question, \"Why farming?\"  This album was his response.\n\nFrom the hard-won grit illuminated in \"The Blues Under My Nails\" and \"The Self-Made Man's Repose,\" to the earnest transformation of \"The Daily Grind, Redeemed,\" this album charts a course from demanding early years to a contemplative retirement. It pays homage to his father in \"Blues for John,\" while unflinchingly exploring personal reckonings in \"Dust on the Old Bible\" and the hard-won wisdom of \"The Unwritten Creed.\"\n\nThrough tracks like \"Footprints in the Dust\" and \"The Four-Legged Philosophers,\" \"Quiet Harvest\" celebrates the enduring bonds and simple joys found in loyal companionship. It delves into the profound tranquility of \"The Quiet Spaces,\" the purposeful work of \"Mending the Ground,\" and the long-term vision of \"Growing a Legacy\" on the land. The album closes by gazing towards \"The Unseen Horizon,\" embracing the mysteries of aging and a rapidly changing world.\n\n\"Quiet Harvest\" is more than just music; it's a testament to life's continuous unfolding, a balm for the soul, and an invitation to find your own profound beauty in the journey from bustling streets to serene fields.\n\n#QuietHarvest #TheShadyRiverBard #CountryBlues #LifeJourney #HomesteadLife #RetirementLife #Wisdom #PersonalGrowth #NewAlbum #Storytelling #EarnedPeace #LifeReflections #FromDustToDawn",
