      "title": "Yo Ho Ho and a Pocket Full of Greed",
      "status": "released",
      "youtube_url": "https://www.youtube.com/playlist?list=PLO_tWXIGUXcHr2R6eMk1Xd3DPGh4fPYtK",
      "description": "Welcome aboard \"Yo Ho Ho and a Pocket Full of Greed,\" the seventeenth album from The Shady River Bard. This is not just a collection of songs; it is a work of historical inversion and a call to consciousness, using the rebellious, democratic spirit of historical pirates as a lens to critique the systemic piracy of the 21st century.\nThe album's title itself is a cynical twist on a children's nursery rhyme, capturing the core tension of the work: the rollicking, romanticized energy of the \"Yo Ho Ho\" myth clashing with the cold, hard reality of \"a Pocket Full of Greed.\" We embark on a four-act narrative voyage that explores the vast ocean of modern corruption. Act I introduces the \"New Buccaneers\"\u2014the CEOs, financiers, and defense contractors who captain our modern vessel, revealing the scale of their plunder and the cynical logic that guides them. Act II takes us \"Below Decks,\" where the devastating human cost of this greed is rendered in visceral, heartbreaking detail, from the dehumanizing pace of the digital sweatshop to the quiet desperation of a family held ransom by an unaffordable cure.\nBut where there is oppression, there is rebellion. Act III, \"The Storm and the Reckoning,\" is the turning point\u2014a furious mutiny where the crew, pushed to the brink, finds their collective voice. This rebellion is given its moral and intellectual backbone by the ghost of a real, historical pirate captain, Samuel \"Black Sam\" Bellamy. Bellamy, a man who championed a democratic pirate code as a direct response to the tyranny of the wealthy merchants he called \"rascals,\" serves as the album's conscience, judging our modern captains and finding them to be the true villains.\nThe final act, \"A New Code,\" moves from deconstruction to construction. Having overthrown the old captains, the crew gathers to draft \"The Articles,\" a new social contract based on the historical pirate principles of fairness, solidarity, and mutual support. The album concludes not with a final, bloody victory, but with the quiet, determined hope of a new journey beginning, sailing toward a horizon of their own making.\nThis is a meticulously researched allegory, a story of the past used to dissect the present, and a reminder that the most dangerous pirates are not those with a skull and crossbones, but those with a logo and a ledger. Join the crew. Learn the story. It's time to take back the ship.\n#YoHoHoAndAPocketFullOfGreed #TheShadyRiverBard #ProtestSongs #FolkMusic #CorporateGreed #ConceptAlbum #SocialCommentary #PirateHistory #Inequality\n@TheShadyRiverBard",
