      "genre": "Baroque Folk",
      "pitch": "1. The End of Virtue (working title \u2014 retained for its blunt moral clarity)\n\n2. Golden Mirrors & Empty Thrones (evoking the narcissistic spectacle and the hollowing of leadership)\n\nThe End of Virtue is a 13-track concept album by The Shady River Bard that examines the systematic erosion of classical virtues\u2014truthfulness, humility, self-restraint, empathy, and accountability\u2014in contemporary American political leadership, using the public record of Donald J. Trump as the primary case study. The album does not seek partisan score-settling; it treats the subject as a symptom and accelerant of a broader cultural collapse in which spectacle, self-mythologizing, and the rejection of shared reality have displaced character as the measure of fitness for power.\n\nThe listener begins as a witness to the golden-mirror stage (vanity and self-mythologizing), descends through the deliberate construction of alternative realities (lying), the casual bending of rules (cheating as metaphor), the abdication of attention and duty, the weaponization of language and division, and the normalization of shamelessness. Mid-album the focus shifts from the individual to the societal wreckage\u2014fractured trust, polarized citizens, and the quiet death of institutional norms. The final act turns outward: a hard-eyed inventory of the cost and a resolute, non-utopian call to reclaim the virtues that make self-government possible. The ultimate message is that the death of virtue is not inevitable; it is a choice repeated daily, and therefore a choice that can still be refused.",
