      "pitch": "PLEONEXIA: The Acoustic Architecture of Infinite Accumulation\n\nAn Exhaustive Conceptual Framework and Production Guide\n\nThe proposed album, tentatively titled Pleonexia (derived from the Greek concept of an insatiable desire to possess what rightfully belongs to others), serves as a sonic document of the early 21st-century economic fracture. It is not merely a collection of songs but a structured auditory argument that juxtaposes the biological reality of human survival\u2014anchored in the caloric deficits of the Pleistocene Epoch\u2014against the abstract absurdity of modern hyper-wealth, specifically the approximate $500 billion net worth of the \"Technocrat\" archetype (modeled on Elon Musk).\n\nThe narrative arc of the album operates on two simultaneous timelines that eventually collide. The first timeline tracks the \"Pleistocene Saver,\" an immortal entity who has labored and saved since the dawn of behavioral modernity, yet fails to achieve the wealth accumulated by the Technocrat in a single lifetime. The second timeline follows the Technocrat's ascent, fueled by public subsidies and the \"ladder-pulling\" mechanics of the Department of Government Efficiency (DOGE), culminating in a frantic escape to Mars while the social safety net on Earth collapses.",
